      },
      "worked": "There are two identical As and seven other distinct letters. Count cases according to the number of As chosen. Five distinct letters have $4!$ circular arrangements; with two identical As, there are $4!/2!$.\n\nNo As:\n$$\\begin{align*}N_0&=\\binom{7}{5}\\times4!\\\\N_0&=504.\\end{align*}$$\n\nOne A:\n$$\\begin{align*}N_1&=\\binom{7}{4}\\times4!\\\\N_1&=840.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTwo As:\n$$\\begin{align*}N_2&=\\binom{7}{3}\\times\\frac{4!}{2!}\\\\N_2&=420.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAdd the three disjoint cases:\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=504+840+420\\\\N&=1764.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
